-- MATHEMATICAL REDUCTION
--
-- Round85 assumed directly that cutoff charges acting on local-core vectors are
-- eventually constant.  Local QFT gives a sharper proof-facing decomposition.
-- For a local observable A and nested cutoffs r <= R, write the larger cutoff
-- commutator as
--
--     [Q_R,A] = [Q_r,A] + [Q_{R\r},A].
--
-- Once r contains supp(A), locality/current conservation should force the outer
-- shell commutator to vanish.  Pure algebra then gives exact cutoff independence
-- of [Q_R,A].  If the vacuum contribution has been removed/neutralized so that
--
--     Q_R (A Omega) = [Q_R,A] Omega,
